  兵贵神速 | bīng guì shén sù | speed is precious in warfare; act with rapid dispatch
  厉兵秣马 | lì bīng mò mǎ | hone weapons and feed horses; prepare intensively for battle
  短兵相接 | duǎn bīng xiāng jiē | engage in hand-to-hand combat; fight at close quarters
  按兵不动 | àn bīng bù dòng | hold troops back; bide one's time without taking action

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  士 | shì | scholar; soldier; gentleman | letrado; caballero; militar | 士 | scholar / warrior | 士 (upright male warrior/official) | "" | 3 | 单一结构 | Ancient bronze pictogram of an axe or ceremonial battle weapon standing upright, symbolizing martial status and noble duty. | An upright, resolute warrior stands tall with broad shoulders (top long stroke) anchored on the firm ground (bottom short stroke) (士). | Un guerrero noble y resuelto se alza firme con anchos hombros y pisada sólida sobre la tierra (士). | 51 | J | 
  兵 | bīng | soldier; weapons; warfare | soldado; arma; tropa | 八 | eight / separate | 八 (two hands) | 斤 (jīn, axe / halberd) | 7 | 上下结构 | Ancient pictogram depicting two hands 八 holding a battle-axe 斤, directly representing armed martial combat. | Two hands (八) gripping a sharp battle-axe (斤) ready to defend the frontier like a brave soldier (兵). | Dos manos resueltas (八) empuñando un hacha de combate (斤) listas para defender la frontera como un soldado (兵). | 55 | OMC | 

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: An honorable warrior (士) who grips his battle weapon (兵) with courage serves as a valiant soldier (士兵).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Un noble combatiente (士) que empuña su arma de combate (兵) sirve con honor como leal soldado (士兵).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In ancient Zhou society, 士 represented the class of noble scholar-warriors proficient in the Six Arts (六艺). Over centuries, 兵 (hands holding an axe) combined with 士 to denote the modern armed serviceman who unites moral discipline with battlefield prowess.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Falling 4th tone followed by high level 1st tone: 'shì bīng' (51-55). Strike 'shì' downward firmly, then leap into a level, sustained 'bīng'.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[5]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    土 | tǔ | earth; soil | Has a short top horizontal stroke and long bottom stroke
