    丘 | qiū | mound; hill | Has a single top stroke and curved base without 八
    乒 | pīng | ping (onomatopoeia) | Missing the right leg stroke of 兵
    乓 | pāng | pong (onomatopoeia) | Missing the left leg stroke of 兵
  etymological_cognates[5]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    仕 | shì | serve as an official
    志 | zhì | ambition; will; aspiration
    斤 | jīn | axe; catty (weight unit)
    斩 | zhǎn | decapitate; chop with an axe
    斧 | fǔ | battle-axe; hatchet

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 士兵 specifically designates an enlisted fighter or rank-and-file private, contrasted with commanders and officers.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 士兵 vs. 将军 | jiāngjūn | 士兵 are the rank-and-file enlisted troops carrying out battlefield orders, whereas 将军 is a high-ranking general responsible for overarching strategic command.
    2 | 士兵 vs. 军人 | jūnrén | 士兵 refers specifically to lower-rank enlisted personnel, whereas 军人 is a comprehensive umbrella term for any service member regardless of rank or role.
    3 | 士兵 vs. 战士 | zhànshì | 士兵 is an objective military rank/role descriptor, while 战士 carries an emotional, heroic, or ideological connotation of a brave fighter.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 边境线上的哨所高耸入云，呼啸的风雪吞没了漫漫长夜。年轻的士兵手握钢枪，宛如一尊巍然屹立的界碑。为了身后万家灯火的安宁，他们将最美好的青春岁月默默奉献给祖国苍茫的边关。 | Biānjìngxiàn shàng de shàosuǒ gāosǒng-rùyún, hūxiào de fēngxuě tūnmò le mànmàn chángyè. Niánqīng de shìbīng shǒuwò gāngqiāng, wǎnrú yì zūn wēirán yìlì de jièbēi. Wèile shēnhòu wànjiā-dēnghuǒ de ānníng, tāmen jiāng zuì měihǎo de qīngchūn suìyuè mòmò fèngxiàn gěi zǔguó cāngmáng de biānguān. | The outpost atop the border ridge pierces the clouds as howling blizzards swallow the long night. Clasping his steel rifle, the young soldier stands like a towering milestone. To protect the peaceful hearths behind him, he silently dedicates his youth to the nation's rugged frontier. | El puesto fronterizo se eleva entre las nubes mientras la ventisca azota la noche. El joven soldado empuña su fusil erguido como un hito inamovible. Para salvaguardar la paz de miles de hogares, entrega en silencio sus mejores años a la austera linde de la patria.
  #2 | 在现代信息化战场上，士兵的角色正在经历深刻变革。除了过硬的身体素质与意志力，现代士兵更需要熟练掌握先进的数字化武器系统，具备在复杂电磁环境下独立判断与协同作战的综合素养。 | Zài xiàndài xìnxīhuà zhànchǎng shàng, shìbīng de juésè zhèngzài jīnglì shēnkè biàngé. Chúle guòyìng de shēntǐ sùzhì yǔ yìzhìlì, xiàndài shìbīng gèng xūyào shúliàn zhǎangwò xiānjìn de shùzìhuà wǔqì xìtǒng, jùbèi zài fùzá diàncí huánjìng xià dúlì pànduàn yǔ xiétóng zuòzhàn de zōnghé sùyǎng. | On modern digitalized battlefields, the soldier's role is undergoing profound transformation. Beyond formidable physical fitness and willpower, modern soldiers must master advanced digital weaponry, possessing capabilities for independent judgment and synchronized combat in complex scenarios. | En los escenarios bélicos digitalizados de hoy, el cometido del soldado experimenta una honda transformación. Además de temple y resistencia física, requiere dominio de sistemas cibernéticos y armamento avanzado, aunando criterio autónomo y作战 coordinada en entornos complejos.
